---
title: How to create a task inside a deal
sidebar:
  order: 11
---
**To add a task to a deal in Taskip, follow these steps:**

![](image-31-1024x476.png)

### **1. Navigate to the Deal**

- Go to the **Sales Pipeline** and click on the deal you want to add a task to. This will open the detailed view of the deal.

### **2. Access the Tasks Tab**

- In the deal view, click on the Tasks tab, which is located next to **Meetings**, **Notes**, and **Activity**.

### **3. Create a New Task**

- Click the + Create Task button, which is located in the top-right corner of the task section.

### **4. Fill in Task Details**

- A pop-up will appear to create a new task. Fill in the following details:
  - **Task Name**: Enter a brief name for the task (e.g., “Call to Prospect”).
  - **Task Type:** Select the type of task (e.g., Call, Meeting, etc.).
  - **Assignee**: Assign the task to a specific team member.
  - **Priority**: Set the priority for the task (Low, Medium, High).
  - **Select Date:** Choose the due date for the task.
  - **Select Time**: Optionally, choose a specific time for the task.
  - **Description**: Add any relevant details or instructions for the task.

![](image-32-843x1024.png)

### **5. Set a Reminder (Optional):**

Taskip allows you to set reminders for tasks to ensure that important deadlines and follow-ups are not missed. The available reminder options are:

- **At task due time:** You’ll be reminded when the task is due.
- **30 min before:** A reminder will be sent 30 minutes before the task’s due time.
- **1 hour before:** A reminder will be sent 1 hour before the task’s due time.
- **1 day before:** You’ll get a reminder 1 day in advance.
- **1 week before:** A reminder will be sent 1 week before the due date.
- **Custom date:** You can set a custom reminder date based on your preferences.

![](image-33-1024x538.png)

Reminders help ensure that your team stays on top of important tasks and deadlines, improving productivity and reducing the chances of forgetting critical actions.

### **6. Set a Repeat (Optional):**

The Repeat functionality allows you to set tasks that occur on a recurring basis. When you setup a repeat task system will automatically create a task for you in that certain time. The available options for repeating tasks are:

![](image-34-1024x593.png)

- **No Repeat**: The task will not repeat.
- **Every Week**: The task will repeat weekly.
- **Every Two Week**: The task will repeat every two weeks.
- **Every Month**: The task will repeat monthly.
- **Every Three Month:** The task will repeat every three months.
- **Every Four Month**: The task will repeat every four months.
- **Every Six Month:** The task will repeat every six months.
- **Every Year**: The task will repeat annually.

Setting tasks to repeat is useful for regular follow-ups, meetings, or other periodic activities, ensuring consistency in your workflow.

These features help manage ongoing tasks and deadlines efficiently, enabling teams to stay organized and proactive.

### **7. Save the Task**

- After filling in the task details, click **Save** to add the task to the deal.

#### **Insight:**

Adding tasks to deals helps you stay organized by ensuring that important activities and follow-ups are planned and assigned to the right person. Tasks keep your team on track, ensuring that no crucial step is missed in progressing a deal.
